(Adaptive Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Resource-Constrained Academic Question Answering) Tj T*
(Authors: Dr. Ananya Rao, Prof. Vikram Menon, and Siddharth Kulkarni) Tj T*
(Department of Computer Science & Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Madras) Tj T*
(Published in: Proceedings of the International Conference on Applied Agentic Systems \(ICAAS 2025\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ABSTRACT) Tj T*
(Large Language Models \(LLMs\) demonstrate strong generative fluency yet remain prone to factual) Tj T*
(hallucinations when queried on specialized academic literature not present in pre-training corpora.) Tj T*
(Standard Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) mitigates this issue by retrieving fixed top-k text) Tj T*
(chunks for every incoming query. However, static retrieval introduces unnecessary latency on simple) Tj T*
(queries and insufficient context coverage on multi-hop technical questions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In this paper, we propose ARAG-Lite \(Adaptive Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Academic) Tj T*
(Documents\), a multi-agent pipeline combining lightweight intent classification, dynamic chunk) Tj T*
(sizing, and ReAct-style self-reflection. Evaluated across 420 peer-reviewed computer science) Tj T*
(papers and 1,800 examiner-style viva questions, ARAG-Lite improves citation faithfulness by 18.4%) Tj T*
(over fixed-k RAG while reducing average token overhead by 27.2% and end-to-end latency by 31.5%.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. INTRODUCTION) Tj T*
(Academic researchers, postgraduate students, and examiners routinely process dense 10-to-30 page) Tj T*
(research manuscripts under tight time constraints. Preparing structured lecture slides and viva) Tj T*
(voce defense questions manually requires extracting problem formulations, algorithmic workflows,) Tj T*
(empirical tables, and limitations without distorting original author claims.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Conventional summarization pipelines feed entire documents into long-context models, which leads) Tj T*
(to "lost-in-the-middle" degradation when key experimental baselines reside on intermediate pages.) Tj T*
(Conversely, naive RAG architectures trigger vector similarity searches indiscriminately—even when) Tj T*
(a user requests a high-level structural synthesis—and fail to verify whether retrieved chunks) Tj T*
(genuinely support generated claims.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
