(1.1 Research Problem Statement) Tj T*
(Existing document-grounded assistants suffer from three interconnected bottlenecks:) Tj T*
(1\) Hallucinated Extrapolation: Generative models frequently invent baseline numbers, dataset) Tj T*
(sizes, or future work items that do not appear in the source manuscript.) Tj T*
(2\) Static Retrieval Blindness: Fixed top-k cosine similarity retrieval cannot distinguish between) Tj T*
(global structural queries \(e.g., summarizing contributions\) and localized factoid queries \(e.g.,) Tj T*
(checking Table 2 hyperparameter values\).) Tj T*
(3\) Unstructured Pedagogical Output: Standard Q&A systems fail to scaffold explanations across) Tj T*
(cognitive difficulty tiers suitable for viva examination preparation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1.2 Research Objectives) Tj T*
(The primary objectives of this work are:) Tj T*
(- Objective 1: Design an intent-driven multi-agent router that classifies academic tasks into) Tj T*
(  summarization, concept extraction, slide synthesis, viva generation, and grounded Q&A.) Tj T*
(- Objective 2: Implement page-aware overlapping chunking paired with dense vector indexing) Tj T*
(  to preserve exact provenance metadata \([Page X]\) for every generated claim.) Tj T*
(- Objective 3: Introduce a ReAct-based faithfulness verification loop that rejects unsupported) Tj T*
(  claims when cosine similarity falls below an empirical grounding threshold \(tau = 0.42\).) Tj T*
(- Objective 4: Benchmark ARAG-Lite against Zero-Shot LLM and Fixed-K RAG baselines.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. LITERATURE REVIEW) Tj T*
(Lewis et al. \(2020\) formalized Retrieval-Augmented Generation by coupling parametric sequence-to-) Tj T*
(sequence models with non-parametric dense passage retrieval over Wikipedia. Subsequent work by) Tj T*
(Asai et al. \(2023\) introduced Self-RAG, training models to emit reflection tokens indicating) Tj T*
(retrieval necessity. While Self-RAG improves factuality on open-domain QA, it requires fine-tuning) Tj T*
(7B-13B parameter weights, making deployment impractical in university labs.) Tj T*
(Gao et al. \(2024\) surveyed modular RAG architectures and highlighted query routing and) Tj T*
(reranking as decisive factors in domain-specific precision. Building on LangChain Expression) Tj T*
(Language \(LCEL\), recent agentic workflows compose PromptTemplates, structured output parsers,) Tj T*
(and vector stores without weight fine-tuning. However, prior systems lack unified multi-agent) Tj T*
(orchestration tailored specifically to academic slide generation and viva evaluation.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
