(3. PROPOSED METHODOLOGY & SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE) Tj T*
(ARAG-Lite operates as a four-stage deterministic-plus-agentic pipeline:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stage 1: Page-Aware PDF Ingestion & Recursive Chunking) Tj T*
(Incoming PDF documents are parsed page-by-page using PyMuPDF \(fitz\) to retain exact physical) Tj T*
(page indices. Text is normalized to strip running headers and segmented using a recursive) Tj T*
(character splitter with chunk size C = 900 characters and overlap O = 150 characters. Each) Tj T*
(chunk stores metadata: {document_id, page_number, chunk_index, section_hint}.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stage 2: Dense Vector Embedding & Isolated Collection Indexing) Tj T*
(Each chunk is encoded into a 768-dimensional dense vector using Gemini Embedding-2 \(or) Tj T*
(all-MiniLM-L6-v2 for offline deployments\) and persisted inside a document-isolated ChromaDB) Tj T*
(collection. Isolation guarantees zero cross-paper contamination when multiple papers are active.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stage 3: Few-Shot Intent Detection & Agent Routing) Tj T*
(User requests pass through an LCEL Intent Router \(FewShotPromptTemplate | LLM | JSONParser\)) Tj T*
(which classifies the request into six intents: SUMMARIZE_PAPER, EXTRACT_CONCEPTS,) Tj T*
(GENERATE_SLIDES, GENERATE_VIVA, ASK_PAPER_QUESTION, and EVALUATE_VIVA_ANSWER.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stage 4: Specialized LCEL Agents & ReAct Grounding Loop) Tj T*
(- Summarizer Agent: Synthesizes abstract, problem statement, objectives, methodology, and) Tj T*
(  conclusions using map-reduce section prompts.) Tj T*
(- Concept-Extractor Agent: Extracts algorithms, formal definitions, contributions, and glossary.) Tj T*
(- Slide-Generator Agent: Produces 8-12 structured 16:9 slides with speaker notes and charts.) Tj T*
(- Viva Agent: Generates multi-difficulty examiner questions and evaluates student responses) Tj T*
(  against retrieved ground-truth passages using rubric-guided reflection.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
