(3.1 ReAct Faithfulness Reflection Algorithm) Tj T*
(For every user question Q in Research Paper Chat, the RAG Chat Agent executes a 4-step loop:) Tj T*
(Step 1 \(Thought\): Determine whether Q requires localized evidence retrieval or document metadata.) Tj T*
(Step 2 \(Action\): Query ChromaDB collection with cosine similarity search for top-k = 5 chunks.) Tj T*
(Step 3 \(Observation\): Inspect retrieved similarity scores S = {s_1, ..., s_k} and page tags.) Tj T*
(Step 4 \(Reflection & Response\): If max\(S\) < 0.35 or evidence is absent, explicitly state that) Tj T*
(the paper does not contain the requested information. Otherwise synthesize an answer citing) Tj T*
(exact page references [Page P].) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS) Tj T*
(The reference prototype is implemented with a FastAPI REST backend \(Python 3.11\) and a React) Tj T*
(TypeScript client. Prompt orchestration uses LangChain Expression Language \(LCEL\) chains of the) Tj T*
(form `prompt | chat_model | pydantic_output_parser`. PowerPoint decks are compiled natively) Tj T*
(in 16:9 widescreen format \(13.333 x 7.5 inches\) using python-pptx with speaker notes attached) Tj T*
(to each slide XML node. The embedding batch processor enforces exponential backoff \(base 500ms,) Tj T*
(max 3 retries\) to handle API rate limits gracefully.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS AND DISCUSSION) Tj T*
(We evaluated ARAG-Lite on the ScholarBench-420 dataset comprising 420 arXiv papers across) Tj T*
(Machine Learning, Distributed Systems, and Cybersecurity, paired with 1,800 human-verified) Tj T*
(viva questions. Three configurations were compared:) Tj T*
(1\) Zero-Shot Full-Text LLM \(no retrieval routing\)) Tj T*
(2\) Fixed-K Standard RAG \(k = 4, no ReAct reflection\)) Tj T*
(3\) ARAG-Lite \(Intent Router + Dynamic k = 5 + ReAct Faithfulness Guard\)) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
