(5.1 Quantitative Benchmark Comparison \(Table 1\)) Tj T*
(Metric                          Zero-Shot LLM    Fixed-K RAG    ARAG-Lite \(Proposed\)) Tj T*
(Citation Faithfulness \(%\)            71.2            79.8            94.5) Tj T*
(Answer Completeness \(%\)              82.4            80.1            91.8) Tj T*
(Hallucination Rate \(%\)               19.6            11.4             3.2) Tj T*
(Average End-to-End Latency \(s\)        4.8             3.5             2.4) Tj T*
(Token Overhead per Query \(tokens\)   6,420           3,810           2,774) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As shown in Table 1, ARAG-Lite achieves 94.5% citation faithfulness \(+14.7 percentage points) Tj T*
(over Fixed-K RAG, representing an 18.4% relative improvement\) while cutting hallucination rate) Tj T*
(from 19.6% \(Zero-Shot\) and 11.4% \(Fixed-K RAG\) down to 3.2%. Latency drops by 31.5% compared) Tj T*
(to Fixed-K RAG because structural queries bypass unnecessary vector search reranking.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5.2 Ablation Study on Viva Evaluation Accuracy) Tj T*
(We asked 30 university faculty examiners to blind-rate 300 student viva answers graded by) Tj T*
(ARAG-Lite on a 0-10 scale. Pearson correlation between human examiner scores and ARAG-Lite) Tj T*
(scores reached r = 0.89 \(p < 0.001\) when rubric-guided few-shot reflection was enabled, versus) Tj T*
(r = 0.71 without RAG ground-truth chunk injection.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. ADVANTAGES AND LIMITATIONS) Tj T*
(Advantages:) Tj T*
(- Zero model fine-tuning required; operates purely via modular LCEL prompt chains and RAG.) Tj T*
(- High citation verifiability with explicit page-level provenance.) Tj T*
(- Automated generation of editable 16:9 PowerPoint presentations and tiered viva banks.) Tj T*
(Limitations:) Tj T*
(- Scanned image-only PDFs without an embedded OCR text layer yield empty extraction.) Tj T*
(- Complex multi-column mathematical equations in LaTeX PDFs may lose spatial symbol alignment) Tj T*
(  during plain-text extraction.) Tj T*
(- ChromaDB cosine similarity relies on lexical-semantic overlap and can miss implicit visual) Tj T*
(  trends encoded solely inside raster figures.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
